---
description: Record falsifiable showwork claims and close through the exit gate.
alwaysApply: true
---

# showwork

Start material work with:

    python -m showwork start --session cursor-<task-slug> --agent cursor

Set SHOWWORK_SESSION=cursor-<task-slug> in the same shell.

Before completion claims, declare the acceptance tests for the user's request:

    python -m showwork require --session cursor-<task-slug> --id regression --scope behavior --description "<behavior tested>" --type command --command-arg python --command-arg scripts/run_tests.py --expect-exit 0 --stdout-contains passed

Test the real changed path, including a failing negative case. Use artifact scope
only for file observations. A matching string does not certify behavior or tests.

After each completed change, record a claim that can fail:

    python -m showwork claim --session cursor-<task-slug> --claim "<what changed>" --type file_contains --path <file> --pattern "<regex>"

Prefer git_state or glob_count when they fit. For tests:

    python -m showwork claim --session cursor-<task-slug> --claim "tests pass" --type command --command-arg python --command-arg scripts/run_tests.py --expect-exit 0 --stdout-contains passed

Before reporting success:

    python -m showwork finish --session cursor-<task-slug> --status ok

If finish exits 2, the claimed done is not real. Fix the gap or retract the claim. Never pass --no-verify to manufacture a clean close.

Commit .showwork/ with the work, then run:

    python -m showwork gate --session cursor-<task-slug> --require-tracked

The gate covers declared checks only. Review omitted requirements and test
adequacy separately. Never use --checks-only as an outcome completion.
